00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
(music) It was a long journey, but at last we reached the place they promised us.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This town has changed completely from the one I remember.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
The old buildings, the dusty roads, everything speaks of history.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Rebin: Halale, do you remember that summer when we used to play here?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Halale: Yes, I remember. Mother always told us not to go far.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Rebin: But we always sneaked off to the river anyway.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Halale: Is that river still there? I can't believe it.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Rebin: Let's go and see. The path is this way.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
(birds singing) The sky is so clear and beautiful today.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Halale: I remember that big tree, it shaded the house of grandfather.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Rebin: They say grandfather planted it, and it remembers everything.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Halale: So today we get to see the places of our childhood?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Rebin: Not just see them, but live inside our memories.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
(a distant voice) Who is that over there? A stranger or someone we know?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Halale: I am holding my breath. I can't tell who it is.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Rebin: Don't be afraid. Stay close to me.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The man: Hello! Aren't you the children of Uncle Rasool?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Rebin: Yes, I am Rebin, and this is my sister Halale.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
The man: I am Dayar, your mother's older brother. I barely recognized your voices.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Halale: Uncle! Is that really you? It's been so many years!

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Dayar: Decades, but I would still know this house anywhere.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Rebin: How are mother and father? Tell them we have arrived.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Dayar: Be quiet, I want to surprise you. They gave me this.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Halale: What is it? It looks strange.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Dayar: It is the key to the old house, the one father left behind.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Rebin: So tonight we are staying in that house?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Dayar: If you let me, you can visit your own rooms.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
(the door creaks open) The sound and scent of wood welcome us.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Halale: That is mother's portrait on the wall.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Rebin: And here is grandfather, young, with his sister.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Dayar: They live here every day, in the soul of this house.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Halale: I want to read those books, the ones on the table.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Rebin: That book is a thousand years old, mother loved it.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Dayar: Now, welcome to your home, to your history.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.000
(fire crackling) The fire spreads through the hearth.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Halale: It is so warm and calm. I feel like I've come home.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Rebin: In the chaos of the big city, I had forgotten all this.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Dayar: The city has changed, but the heart of this valley never does.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Halale: So what is our plan for tonight?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Rebin: Let's tell our stories to each other, like before.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Dayar: I will prepare Kurdish tea, with fresh village bread.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Halale: The smell of that tea takes me back to my childhood.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.000
(a sound outside) The cows move, everything stays as it was.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Rebin: Do mother and father know we are here?

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Dayar: No, they asked me to wait, they want to surprise you.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Halale: A surprise? Are they in the town?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Dayar: Yes, they came tonight, for you.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.000
(the door opens) Two familiar figures appear in the doorway.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Mother: Rebin! Halale! My children!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Halale: Mother! I have been longing for this moment!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Father: My son, did you come to live with us?

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Rebin: Yes, father, so that there is a return, so that history continues.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Mother: I have been waiting for this day since you left.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Father: A home never dies, as long as you come back to it.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.000
(traditional music) The sound of the tanbur rises from the next room.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Halale: This melody, the scent of these nights, it all feels like a dream.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
Rebin: But it is no dream, it is all real.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Mother: Let's sit at the table where grandfather used to sit.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Father: This table has seen many generations of joy and sorrow.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Dayar: I am serving the bread, with home-made yogurt and herbs.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Halale: This food is a rich way of remembering who we are.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Rebin: In the big city I had forgotten these tastes, but I never forgot them.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Mother: Now that you are back, stay a while, with us.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Father: We are ready to keep this house alive for you every day.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Halale: Mother, I will never leave again.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Rebin: Me too, this valley is part of who I am.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.000
(the fire) The flame is reflected in their eyes.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Dayar: Let us make a promise: to protect this tradition for future generations.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.000
Father: A promise, on all our hands.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.000
(the tanbur fades out) A peaceful silence.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Mother: This night must stay in our memory, forever.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Rebin: I will write this night down, like a book.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Halale: I will record this melody, so the children can hear the sound.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Father: This is a beginning, not an end.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Mother: Welcome home, to the valley we love most.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
(sunrise) The morning light touches the building.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Rebin: A new day, a new feeling.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Halale: And with that day, my return to myself is complete.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Dayar: We will build all these dreams along this road.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
(closing music) The end.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
